WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.600
Refund extraction looks simple, until the model picks the wrong

00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:04.000
date.

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.088
RouteWise helps developers choose a cheaper model setup, backed by

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:08.662
evidence.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.638
Here’s a recorded synthetic example.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.912
The old route misses the refund date.

00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:18.538
RouteWise reads “this Friday” against the store’s timestamp, and gets

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.812
April twenty-fourth.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.600
If the date is ambiguous, it holds the answer for

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:24.088
review.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.950
You can inspect the source, raw response, and every check.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.712
Choose your accuracy and response-time targets.

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:36.988
RouteWise compares NVIDIA Nemotron models on Nebius Token Factory, then

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.612
picks the cheapest setup the evidence supports.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:44.962
On three hundred twelve synthetic conversations, this setup completed ninety-eight

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:49.388
point four percent correctly without review, with no incorrect answers

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.012
released.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.338
Need a faster response?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.975
The recommendation switches to Super.

00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:58.300
Ask for more certainty than the data supports, and it

00:00:58.312 --> 00:00:59.362
recommends nothing.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.162
This call was captured while recording.

00:01:02.525 --> 00:01:06.475
Nano leaves the date blank; RouteWise resolves it to April

00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:07.062
sixth.

00:01:07.425 --> 00:01:11.300
The trace includes the actual response time and every model-call

00:01:11.312 --> 00:01:11.825
charge.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.550
At a million requests a month, recorded inference costs project

00:01:16.562 --> 00:01:20.638
to about eighty dollars, versus three hundred forty-nine for Super.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.350
Hosting and human review cost extra.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.800
Download the decision and integration recipe.

00:01:27.162 --> 00:01:29.112
These results use synthetic data.

00:01:29.475 --> 00:01:33.350
Independent human validation is still pending, and the latest noise

00:01:33.362 --> 00:01:35.625
test missed its response-time target.

00:01:35.988 --> 00:01:39.388
RouteWise shows those limits alongside its recommendation.
